{"id": "EUVD-2026-87234", "enisaUuid": "36621540-f8b5-3c39-8969-c08fc9a73188", "description": "RabbitMQ is a messaging and streaming broker. From 4.0.0 until 4.0.22 and 4.1.14 and 4.2.7, Admin-only atom exhaustion: PUT /api/users tags list. settags/2 maps rabbitdatacoercion:toatom/1 over the user's tags list. The 20 MB management body limit fits ~3-4M short tag strings. An administrator can crash the node in a single request by creating a user (or importing definitions) with ~1M unique tag administrator. This issue is fixed in versions 4.0.22 and 4.1.14 and 4.2.7.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T16:29:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T19:55:13", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/security/advisories/GHSA-34c7-r8w9-5wv8", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/commit/86601c5a6d1c7e41060e3dbd165c88bdc91266ee", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/releases/tag/v4.2.7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-67226"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "aad73cc8-e091-3daa-8162-d301bf2b3e59", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0, < 4.2.7"}, {"id": "ba48cbc3-3049-334e-8c89-572302b670a6", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.1.0, < 4.1.14"}, {"id": "e87b90c0-613a-3c8d-8892-c19da2c6727d", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0, < 4.0.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5be38719-a562-30ed-8e77-ddf8bbecf533", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}], "isExploited": false}